==English==

===Verb===
{{head|en|verb|head=[[pay]] [[through]] [[the]] [[nose]]}}

# {{context|idiomatic|lang=en}} To pay a [[high]] [[price]], especially an [[exorbitant]] or [[excessive]] amount, either in [[money]] or in some other manner.
#* '''1918''', [[w:Peter_B._Kyne|Peter B. Kyne]], ''The Valley of the Giants'', ch. 36:
#*:"You'll '''pay through the nose''' for this, you scoundrel," Sexton whimpered. "I'll fix you, you traitor."
#* '''1921''', [[w:John_Galsworthy|John Galsworthy]], ''The Forsyte Saga'', part 2, ch. 4:
#*: That fellow would milk the settlements somehow, and make his family '''pay through the nose''' to keep him out of bankruptcy.

